{{!
    @template local_payments/price_changed

    Shown when the price moved between the buyer opening checkout and confirming it (AC-4.13.6) —
    almost always an automatic offer that reached its end date while they were deciding. Nothing
    has been charged and no gateway session exists at this point; the buyer either accepts the
    revised price, which re-submits the same checkout with the new figure as the agreed one, or
    walks away.

    The old price is struck through rather than merely mentioned, because the one thing this screen
    has to make unmissable is that the number is not the one they were looking at a moment ago.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * item_name - What is being bought
    * old_amount_formatted - The price the buyer was quoted, with currency
    * new_amount_formatted - The price now, with currency
    * increase - true when the new price is higher (drives the wording + colour)
    * action - Where the confirmation form posts
    * sesskey - Session key
    * fields - Hidden fields to carry through: {name, value}
    * cancel_url - Back to where they came from

    Example context (json):
    {
        "item_name": "Advanced Accounting",
        "old_amount_formatted": "210.00 EGP",
        "new_amount_formatted": "350.00 EGP",
        "increase": true,
        "action": "#",
        "sesskey": "abc123",
        "cancel_url": "#",
        "fields": [
            {"name": "courseid", "value": "9"},
            {"name": "coupon_code", "value": ""}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="lp-pricechanged">
    <h3 class="lp-pricechanged__title">{{#str}} pricechanged_title, local_payments {{/str}}</h3>

    <p class="lp-pricechanged__lead">
        {{#increase}}{{#str}} pricechanged_up, local_payments {{/str}}{{/increase}}
        {{^increase}}{{#str}} pricechanged_down, local_payments {{/str}}{{/increase}}
    </p>

    <div class="lp-pricechanged__box">
        <div class="lp-pricechanged__item">{{item_name}}</div>
        <div class="lp-pricechanged__row">
            <span class="lp-pricechanged__label">{{#str}} pricechanged_was, local_payments {{/str}}</span>
            <s class="lp-pricechanged__old">{{old_amount_formatted}}</s>
        </div>
        <div class="lp-pricechanged__row lp-pricechanged__row--now">
            <span class="lp-pricechanged__label">{{#str}} pricechanged_now, local_payments {{/str}}</span>
            <strong class="lp-pricechanged__new">{{new_amount_formatted}}</strong>
        </div>
    </div>

    <form method="post" action="{{action}}">
        <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
        {{#fields}}
            <input type="hidden" name="{{name}}" value="{{value}}">
        {{/fields}}

        <div class="lp-pricechanged__actions">
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
                {{#str}} pricechanged_confirm, local_payments {{/str}}
            </button>
            <a href="{{cancel_url}}" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">{{#str}} cancel {{/str}}</a>
        </div>
    </form>
</div>
